estruction of the universe in episode  3. he could see the stones as a way to  get his universe back and christine and  as i mentioned before he definitely has  ultron inside of him at least a part of  him now the watcher sends everybody back  to their respective universes at the  exact point in time where they were  taken away much like an avengers in-game  where steve had to return the infinity  stones to the exact point in time when  they were taken he returns everybody but  natasha in her universe she was the only  person left alive literally the only  person so having her in that universe  probably won't make any difference at  all so he puts her in the universe from  episode 3 the one where natasha actually  died when we last left that episode loki  had pretty much taken control over the  world all of the avengers were dead  except for steve rogers and captain  marvel was called so we go to this  universe and loki with his asgardian  army is fighting captain marvel nick  fury steve rogers and now a new black  widow from a different universe in which  black widow quickly makes easy work of  loki fury realizes that this is not the  same black widow but he's okay with it  then we go to the post credit in which  we are back in peggy carter's universe  natasha tells her to kind of brace  herself in which we find the hydra  stomper that steve rogers used in the  very first episode and natasha tells us  that there's somebody inside of it  telling us basically that steve rogers  is still alive this is also setting up  at least one episode for season two and  like i said i know a lot of people were  expecting some type of a tie-in into the  mcu into multiverse of madness and which  we did not get or did we not directly  but if we read in between the lines we  kind of see that some of this is going  to bleed over recently there was a  leaked photo for doctor strange and the  multiverse of madness concept art showed  that ultron bots will indeed be in the  film also not to mention the illuminati  is supposed to be introduced in doctor  strange in a multiverse of madness as  well and i believe we could have seen  the start of that here because the  illuminati is essentially the guardians  of the multiverse now in the comics they  simply protect the world and their  universe they consist of the leaders of  different groups iron man from the  avengers mr fantastic from the fantastic  four professor xavier from the x-men  black bolt from the inhumans namor the  submariner of atlantis and of course  doctor strange but we know marvel  doesn't always do a complete adaptation  of the comics in fact more often than  not they don't and the illuminati are  also supposed to guard the infinity  stones in which there aren't really any  infinity stones in our main mcu right  now which leads me to believe that the  illuminati are going to be introduced so  they can protect the multiverse they are  coming in multiverse of madness after  all and why would they come and be  formed if it didn't have to do with the  multiverse so in the mcu instead of the  illuminati being protectors of just one  universe i believe they are going to be  protectors of all of them essentially a  guardians of the multiverse but with a  full-time job of protecting the  multiverse now the final thought on this  episode and the series as a whole is not  to forget what the producers of the show  said they did say that this is canon to  the mcu now with the multiverse that  means a lot of things can be canon to  the mcu but the biggest thing to focus  on here is the watcher if the watcher is  canon to the mcu that means that not  only is he the watcher for these  animated universes but he is actually  the watcher for our live action  universes as well meaning that he could  show up in live action form in  multiverse of madness and if that is  possible that means that it is also  possible for any of these other  characters to show up in multiverse of  madness as well in fact it has been  rumored that peggy carter is going to  show up in the movie that's just a rumor  for now but the basic principle of this  of the multiverse is that literally  anything is possible ultron stated that  in episode 8 and marvel even advertised  that in their promos for this final  episode they said that anything is  possible in the multiverse so i would  definitely expect some remnants of what  if to appear in the mcu at some point in  time most likely in multiverse of  madness now i am genuinely curious to  hear what you all had to think about  what if as a series as a whole so let me  know what you rate the entire series in  the comments down below don't forget to  like the video and subscribe so you can  stay up to date on all the latest mcu  news for live updates you can follow me  on instagram and twitter and as always  thank you all so much for watching woof  [Music]  you
 

